id: decisions/031-typed-ids-one-hash-form
title: "Every record an id, one hash spelling"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'identifier-form'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: identifier-form
axis_gloss: "whether identity is carried by a structured, resolvable, namespaced identifier, or a bare string, hash or path"
poles:
  a: structured-addressable-id
  b: bare-opaque-handle
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 8.4
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(10) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Must every record and every cross-reference carry a stable, namespaced
  identifier and one hash format, or may a bare string, path or hex stand in?

why_it_matters: >
  core/canonical-extension.yawn says stable ids and typed relations carry
  identity, not paths, yet the schema set spells hashes two ways and one intake
  template has no id at all. Once answered, a bot that links records knows what
  a reference must contain before it can be trusted, and a child Yawn inherits
  an address it can be found at rather than a filename.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    8 judgments sit at structured-addressable-id (3 authored) and 2 at
    bare-opaque-handle (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Which hash spelling Dave wants canonical, and whether coordinate: must resolve
    over https or is a namespace only.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every active record carries an id. Every cross-reference in a
      machine-read schema is a typed ref (kind and id, plus revision or hash where
      the target is versioned). Hashes carry one spelling everywhere. schemaVersion
      is a namespaced string, never a bare integer.
    cost: "Normalize the hash pattern in either the three state-substrate schemas or the six later ones; migrate ten schemas from schemaVersion const 1 to namespaced strings; add id to templates/conversation-import-draft.yawn."
    risk: "Changing the state-substrate hash spelling breaks 8 passing assertions in tests/state-substrate-v1.test.mjs and any stored hashes."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that every property named *Hash or *Sha256 across schemas/*.json uses one regex; extend the record-spine test to require id on every template."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0216"
      - "J0712"
      - "J0730"
      - "J0838"
      - "J0980"
      - "J1071"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Bare handles are acceptable. A path, a bare hex digest, an integer
      version or a namespace string without a scheme is enough to identify a record
      or a state.
    cost: "Softens core/canonical-extension.yawn relationship_to_identity and core/holarchy.yawn invariants[2]."
    risk: "Two hash formats stay in circulation and a comparison across schema families silently fails."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this."
    evidence_for:
      - "J1072"
      - "J1171"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Every active record carries an id, and machine-read schemas use typed
      refs. One hash spelling is canonical and the other is normalized at the
      boundary; schemaVersion is a namespaced string on every new schema, with the
      ten integer-versioned schemas grandfathered by name until next touched.
      templates/conversation-import-draft.yawn is the one template allowed to lack
      an id, because the id is assigned at routing, and it says so in a field.
    cost: "Pick the hash spelling; add a normalizer; add an assigned_at: routing note to the import draft; write the grandfather list."
    risk: "The grandfather list for integer schemaVersion never shrinks."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that every hash pattern in schemas/*.json matches the chosen regex or the normalizer's accepted input; a test that every template except the named exception carries id; the grandfather list lives in the test and may only shrink."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0216"
      - "J0838"
      - "J0980"
      - "J1071"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.75
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Three authored judgments and the canonical-extension suite (8 assertions)
    implement path-is-not-identity; both opposing judgments are revealed drift,
    not choices. J1072 is a plain split between the older state-substrate schemas
    (sha256:-prefixed, 8 test assertions) and six later schemas (bare hex), so one
    spelling must win and a normalizer covers the other. J1171 has a defensible
    reason, an import draft has no id until routing assigns one, which is worth
    writing down rather than removing. The inference that the prefixed form fits
    J1071's preference for self-describing namespaced strings is mine, not the
    repo's.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "All *Hash and *Sha256 patterns in schemas/*.json match one regex, and a test in tests/ locks it."
    - "templates/conversation-import-draft.yawn either carries id or states in a field that id is assigned at routing."
    - "references/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_RESEARCH_BRAID.yawn coordinate either resolves over https or is marked unresolved."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new schema lands with a third hash format or a bare integer schemaVersion
    and npm test stays green.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0216"
  - "J0712"
  - "J0730"
  - "J0838"
  - "J0980"
  - "J1071"
  - "J1072"
  - "J1171"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
